7.2.2 OLLIVIER-RICCI CURVATURE (ORC)
In an unweighted graph, the neighborhood of each node x, denoted as N (x), is assigned a probability distribution according to a lazy random walk formulation (Lin et al., 2011). Specifically, we define the distribution as follows:
