denoted expp : TpP → P, allows for this transfer. For product manifolds, the exponential map decomposes into individual component exponential maps. Specifically, given a tangent vector v = (v1, v2, . . . , vk) at p = (p1, p2, . . . , pk) ∈ P, the exponential map on P can be expressed as:
expp(v) = (expp1 (v1), expp2 (v2), . . . , exppk (vk)) (12)
